 "header": {
  "title": "Herbort von Fritzlar: 'Liet von Troye' (H) (Heidelberg, Universitätsbibl., Cpg 368): AI translation (Claude)",
  "author": "Herbort von Fritzlar (?)",
  "publisher": "Classica Codex AI translations",
  "date": "2026",
  "source": "Translated by Claude (claude-opus-5-5, Anthropic) from the library's urn:rem:herbort-von-fritzlar:m541h:norm, from the Referenzkorpus Mittelhochdeutsch, ReM 2.1 (CC BY-SA 4.0), one English line for each line of the original. Only some passages are translated so far: those that the Atlas of Ancient Myth, Magic in the Ancient Texts and the demons-and-angels study cite.",
  "statement": "An AI-generated translation. No specialist has reviewed it.",
  "availability": "CC BY-SA 4.0, as its source requires: credit the Referenzkorpus Mittelhochdeutsch, ReM 2.1 and this AI translation, and share adaptations under the same licence."
 },
 "notes": {
  "543": "578-579: 'des was niht, man hette es wân' is read as 'there was nothing in it; people fancied it was so'. It might instead mean that no one doubted it was so.",
  "754": "757: 'reben' taken as 'rave, be out of my wits'.",
  "17629": "17648: 'si wil man über man' is unclear: 'man after man', or perhaps 'every man whatever'. 17673: 'mîn herze mich mir selben nam', literally 'my heart took me from myself', i.e. his resolve overcame his desire.",
  "1011": "1013: 'genante' read as from genenden 'venture, take courage'; it could instead be 'named [it]'. 1037: 'brief', a written document, evidently a charm.",
  "8537": "8537-8538: sense uncertain; taken as the narrator resuming the story where he left it. Briseida is the Briseis named earlier in the poem.",
  "9878": "9882: literally 'his banner', meaning Diomedes's; the silk is Briseida's sleeve (stûche), carried as a token.",
  "1542": "1577-1578: 'gesindelæhe', 'unvlætic' and 'unwæhe' are rendered approximately ('servant-folk', 'unkempt', 'shabby'). 1587: 'ûz der hant', literally 'out of the hand'.",
  "2188": "2188: 'über allen den walt' is read with the next line (the spring's streams rang across the whole forest); it could instead close the previous sentence ('clear and cold beyond any in the forest').",
  "2396": "Piro: Nestor's seat, presumably Pylos.",
  "9363": "9366: 'denne des ir hier bereit sît' is unclear; perhaps 'than you are ready to believe here'.",
  "10394": "10399: 'zuodrant' is uncertain; taken as 'was crushed, broken'.",
  "13534": "13537: 'liebe er im gedâhte' is unclear: 'he thought fondly of him' (of Antilochus), or 'he looked forward to joy'.",
  "15838": "Theanus: here a male priest; in the classical story the keeper of the Palladium is Theano, a priestess."
 },
 "nodes": [
  {
   "ref": "338",
   "text": "and told them to turn away from there."
  },
  {
   "ref": "339",
   "text": "They took the oars in hand"
  },
  {
   "ref": "340",
   "text": "and turned toward the land of Troy."
  },
  {
   "ref": "341",
   "text": "They were in haste for the voyage."
  },
  {
   "ref": "342",
   "text": "A sweet wind came after them,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "343",
   "text": "very good for their ships,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "344",
   "text": "which drove them through the sea's flood"
  },
  {
   "ref": "345",
   "text": "very swiftly"
  },
  {
   "ref": "346",
   "text": "to Troy, into the kingdom"
  },
  {
   "ref": "347",
   "text": "where King Laomedon reigned."
  },
  {
   "ref": "348",
   "text": "Then Hercules and Jason ordered"
  },
  {
   "ref": "349",
   "text": "their sails struck."
  },
  {
   "ref": "350",
   "text": "They had found a harbour"
  },
  {
   "ref": "351",
   "text": "by a little stream,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "352",
   "text": "clear and very pure,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "353",
   "text": "fresh and good in every way."
  },
  {
   "ref": "543",
   "text": "The king had a daughter,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "544",
   "text": "very wise in counsel,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "545",
   "text": "as the book tells me;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "546",
   "text": "she was a very wise maiden,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "547",
   "text": "for she knew well"
  },
  {
   "ref": "548",
   "text": "all kinds of arts"
  },
  {
   "ref": "549",
   "text": "that on earth"
  },
  {
   "ref": "550",
   "text": "could ever be."
  },
  {
   "ref": "551",
   "text": "She knew medicine"
  },
  {
   "ref": "552",
   "text": "and necromancy,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "553",
   "text": "which is called the black books,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "554",
   "text": "in which one finds curses"
  },
  {
   "ref": "555",
   "text": "and conjurations:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "556",
   "text": "how, in wickedness,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "557",
   "text": "one conjures the evil spirits,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "558",
   "text": "so that one learns from them"
  },
  {
   "ref": "559",
   "text": "all that has happened,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "560",
   "text": "and how one can foresee"
  },
  {
   "ref": "561",
   "text": "many a thing that is to come."
  },
  {
   "ref": "562",
   "text": "Even now that art is learned"
  },
  {
   "ref": "563",
   "text": "in a city, at Toledo,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "564",
   "text": "which stands in Spain."
  },
  {
   "ref": "565",
   "text": "The maiden was called Medea."
  },
  {
   "ref": "566",
   "text": "Whether it were far or near,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "567",
   "text": "throughout the land,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "568",
   "text": "whatever human beings may know,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "569",
   "text": "that she could well know;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "570",
   "text": "she had applied herself to it so."
  },
  {
   "ref": "571",
   "text": "She conjured the water so that it went"
  },
  {
   "ref": "572",
   "text": "back to its source"
  },
  {
   "ref": "573",
   "text": "and shot uphill,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "574",
   "text": "though it had once flowed down."
  },
  {
   "ref": "575",
   "text": "By night she conjured the moon"
  },
  {
   "ref": "576",
   "text": "so that it went backward"
  },
  {
   "ref": "577",
   "text": "when it should have gone forward."
  },
  {
   "ref": "578",
   "text": "There was nothing in it; people fancied"
  },
  {
   "ref": "579",
   "text": "that it was so."
  },
  {
   "ref": "580",
   "text": "That is what sorcerers can do,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "581",
   "text": "and sorceresses."
  },
  {
   "ref": "582",
   "text": "Of arts of this kind"
  },
  {
   "ref": "583",
   "text": "the lady knew a great deal,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "584",
   "text": "both in earnest and in play."
  },
  {
   "ref": "585",
   "text": "When Medea heard"
  },
  {
   "ref": "586",
   "text": "that lord Jason had come there,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "754",
   "text": "Can anyone understand that?"
  },
  {
   "ref": "755",
   "text": "That is very strange."
  },
  {
   "ref": "756",
   "text": "I think the elves are deceiving me."
  },
  {
   "ref": "757",
   "text": "Does love make me rave?"
  },
  {
   "ref": "758",
   "text": "No, a spell has been put on me."
  },
  {
   "ref": "759",
   "text": "Yet it is no spell at all;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "760",
   "text": "it comes to me from love."
  },
  {
   "ref": "761",
   "text": "I can tell that well by this:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "762",
   "text": "my heart is like a coal."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1011",
   "text": "that is needed for it;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1012",
   "text": "yet we shall get it."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1013",
   "text": "At once she then ventured [on it];"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1014",
   "text": "she kindled a light;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1015",
   "text": "she brought out an image"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1016",
   "text": "sung over with her prayer,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1017",
   "text": "bewitched and conjured;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1018",
   "text": "it was good against wrath"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1019",
   "text": "and against other fierceness."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1020",
   "text": "She gave it to him; he was glad."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1021",
   "text": "She gave him an ointment"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1022",
   "text": "and told him to smear himself all over"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1023",
   "text": "with it, entirely:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1024",
   "text": "wherever the fire flashed on him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1025",
   "text": "it could do him no harm."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1026",
   "text": "Then out of her chest she gave him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1027",
   "text": "a golden ring"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1028",
   "text": "that was to serve against spells"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1029",
   "text": "and was good against venom and poison,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1030",
   "text": "against the dragon and against the fire's glow."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1031",
   "text": "He found one virtue in it:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1032",
   "text": "whenever he closed it in his hand"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1033",
   "text": "so that on the ring's stone"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1034",
   "text": "no light shone,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1035",
   "text": "this sign befell him:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1036",
   "text": "that no one saw him."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1037",
   "text": "She also gave him a letter;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1038",
   "text": "whoever saw him loved him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1542",
   "text": "and charged at him on the battlefield."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1543",
   "text": "Yet he put himself on the defensive."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1544",
   "text": "Hercules rode among the host;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1545",
   "text": "he struck and trampled;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1546",
   "text": "he waded in the blood."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1547",
   "text": "At last he came charging"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1548",
   "text": "to where he found Laomedon,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1549",
   "text": "sorrowful and in distress;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1550",
   "text": "he struck his head off."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1551",
   "text": "He said, \"Let this be your toll,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1552",
   "text": "which I owe you"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1553",
   "text": "from when I rode through your land"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1554",
   "text": "without doing harm or injury."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1555",
   "text": "What you sent to tell me then"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1556",
   "text": "I remember against you today"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1557",
   "text": "with a wrathful heart;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1558",
   "text": "for that you lie in the blood.\""
  },
  {
   "ref": "1559",
   "text": "He turned his horse around;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1560",
   "text": "by straight ways and crooked"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1561",
   "text": "he rode and charged"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1562",
   "text": "until he had wholly avenged his wrong."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1563",
   "text": "He struck down so many of them"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1564",
   "text": "that for the dead he could scarcely ride"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1565",
   "text": "back into the city."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1566",
   "text": "Those whom on the battlefield"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1567",
   "text": "he could not slay"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1568",
   "text": "had crept into the thickets."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1569",
   "text": "When the battle had been fought,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1570",
   "text": "the Greeks all rode together"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1571",
   "text": "and paced into Troy"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1572",
   "text": "with clamour and with joy,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1573",
   "text": "for nothing more welcome had ever befallen them."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1574",
   "text": "Then they took their ease."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1575",
   "text": "They came with shouting and with sport;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1576",
   "text": "there they found nothing but womenfolk"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1577",
   "text": "and poor servant-folk,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1578",
   "text": "unkempt and shabby,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1579",
   "text": "of base kindred,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1580",
   "text": "and wretched kitchen-boys."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1581",
   "text": "The ladies had fled;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1582",
   "text": "how were they to act?"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1583",
   "text": "They did not know how to bear themselves."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1584",
   "text": "They sat in the temple,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1585",
   "text": "at home, in desolation;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1586",
   "text": "they leaned against the walls,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1587",
   "text": "they bowed their cheeks into their hands;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1588",
   "text": "their clothes were torn,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1589",
   "text": "their headdresses snatched away,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1590",
   "text": "their heads dishevelled,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1591",
   "text": "their hair undressed."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1592",
   "text": "They said, \"Alas, unhappy year,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1593",
   "text": "and alas, unhappy blow,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1594",
   "text": "alas, unhappy day,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1595",
   "text": "alas, unhappy time!"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1596",
   "text": "We have lost on every side;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1597",
   "text": "our kinsmen have been slain."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1598",
   "text": "If we could make sure"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1599",
   "text": "that no wrongful violence"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1600",
   "text": "would be done to us here,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1601",
   "text": "we would lament no more."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1602",
   "text": "Now we are in pain on every side.\""
  },
  {
   "ref": "1603",
   "text": "The lords then came;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1604",
   "text": "they took them by force."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1605",
   "text": "Not one of them was spared"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1606",
   "text": "from having violence done to her."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1607",
   "text": "Telamon took with him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1608",
   "text": "the king's daughter Hesione,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1609",
   "text": "a beautiful young lady;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1610",
   "text": "she was given to him as a reward"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1611",
   "text": "because he charged foremost"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1612",
   "text": "when the city was won."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1613",
   "text": "He was very glad of her."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1614",
   "text": "From that came great grief."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1615",
   "text": "He wanted to have her as a concubine;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1616",
   "text": "that later came to vex her kinsmen."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1617",
   "text": "Dares has written thus:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1618",
   "text": "for a month afterwards they remained"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1619",
   "text": "in Troy, the strangers,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1664",
   "text": "He had five sons and three daughters."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1665",
   "text": "Of the sons, three were called thus:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1666",
   "text": "Hector, Paris, Helenus;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1667",
   "text": "the fourth was called Deiphobus,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "1668",
   "text": "and the fifth Troilus."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1669",
   "text": "They were all men of excellence."
  },
  {
   "ref": "1670",
   "text": "Hector had strength,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2188",
   "text": "all over the forest"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2189",
   "text": "its streams rang out."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2190",
   "text": "There I cooled my tongue;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2191",
   "text": "I splashed my eyes;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2192",
   "text": "I fanned the breeze toward myself."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2193",
   "text": "As I was cooling myself thus,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2194",
   "text": "there came lady Venus,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2195",
   "text": "Pallas and Juno;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2196",
   "text": "their splendour shone so"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2197",
   "text": "that I thought in the spring"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2198",
   "text": "three suns were shining."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2199",
   "text": "They had been sent to me."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2200",
   "text": "They carried an apple in hand;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2201",
   "text": "it was of gold, all red."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2202",
   "text": "Each of them offered me her gift"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2203",
   "text": "so that I would judge"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2204",
   "text": "which among the ladies"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2205",
   "text": "was the most beautiful of all."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2206",
   "text": "Juno offered this honour:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2207",
   "text": "\"I will make you rich forever.\""
  },
  {
   "ref": "2208",
   "text": "Pallas, knowledge and skill;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2209",
   "text": "Venus offered as a reward"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2210",
   "text": "a woman so beautiful"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2211",
   "text": "that nowhere would there be any"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2396",
   "text": "Nestor had sent for him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2397",
   "text": "to come to Piro"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2398",
   "text": "and hear from him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2399",
   "text": "a very good piece of news;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2400",
   "text": "I do not know what it was."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2401",
   "text": "The king was in haste to reach Piro."
  },
  {
   "ref": "2402",
   "text": "His wife was called Helen;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2403",
   "text": "she was the beautiful woman"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2404",
   "text": "whom, as a reward to Paris,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2405",
   "text": "Venus had promised"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2406",
   "text": "for that decision,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "2407",
   "text": "because he awarded her the apple,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8142",
   "text": "So the time passed"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8143",
   "text": "while their truce lasted."
  },
  {
   "ref": "8144",
   "text": "Meanwhile Calchas lamented"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8145",
   "text": "that he had in the city"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8146",
   "text": "a daughter, very constant,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8147",
   "text": "beautiful, courtly and wise,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8148",
   "text": "who was called Briseis;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8149",
   "text": "she could not stay there:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8150",
   "text": "they wanted to drive her out"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8151",
   "text": "on account of their goddess"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8152",
   "text": "whom they had in there."
  },
  {
   "ref": "8153",
   "text": "They complained every day"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8537",
   "text": "Now I have got no further"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8538",
   "text": "than you have heard before:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8539",
   "text": "Troilus and Briseida"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8540",
   "text": "parted there"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8541",
   "text": "with such sorrow"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8542",
   "text": "that, had they been about to die"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8543",
   "text": "and end their lives,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8544",
   "text": "it would have been far better for them."
  },
  {
   "ref": "8545",
   "text": "Menestheus and Telamon"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8546",
   "text": "and lord Tydeus's son,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8547",
   "text": "duke Diomedes,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8548",
   "text": "and the wise Ulysses,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "8549",
   "text": "and many another man"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9363",
   "text": "however it may please you;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9364",
   "text": "it may well be true all the same."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9365",
   "text": "I have read of greater things"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9366",
   "text": "than what you have before you here."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9367",
   "text": "By God's command, at that time,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9368",
   "text": "the devil spoke out of the images"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9369",
   "text": "and foretold whatever came to pass."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9370",
   "text": "He worked many a wonder,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9371",
   "text": "which was written of him."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9372",
   "text": "From that came down to us the magic art"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9373",
   "text": "that is called *nigromantia* [necromancy],"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9374",
   "text": "as you have heard before."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9375",
   "text": "In the chamber lay Hector"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9878",
   "text": "Troilus began the fight"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9879",
   "text": "with Diomedes."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9880",
   "text": "It grieved him sorely"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9881",
   "text": "that his woman's silk"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9882",
   "text": "should be the other's banner."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9883",
   "text": "He saw there by the sleeve"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9884",
   "text": "that his beloved Briseida"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9885",
   "text": "would soon do his will"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9886",
   "text": "or had done it."
  },
  {
   "ref": "9887",
   "text": "They both had great hatred:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9888",
   "text": "Troilus because"
  },
  {
   "ref": "9889",
   "text": "the other wanted to have his woman;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10394",
   "text": "The silk turned red"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10395",
   "text": "that should have been white."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10396",
   "text": "Achilles made it plain"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10397",
   "text": "that he was the stronger."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10398",
   "text": "He threw him onto the grass"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10399",
   "text": "so that he was utterly broken,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10400",
   "text": "and came charging at him;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10401",
   "text": "he struck him and trampled [him];"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10402",
   "text": "in no way did he let him"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10403",
   "text": "raise himself up."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10404",
   "text": "His eyes grew dim,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10405",
   "text": "his nose began to pale;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10406",
   "text": "that was a bitter sign."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10407",
   "text": "His hands went slack;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10408",
   "text": "Hector met his end."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10409",
   "text": "When he saw him die,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10410",
   "text": "Achilles spoke to him thus:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10411",
   "text": "\"May God keep you;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10412",
   "text": "may your soul fare well."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10413",
   "text": "You were, among your kindred,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10414",
   "text": "comfort and joy"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10415",
   "text": "to your friends one and all,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10416",
   "text": "great and small,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10417",
   "text": "poor and rich,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10418",
   "text": "all of them alike,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10419",
   "text": "father, mother, wife, child,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10420",
   "text": "brother, sister, and those there are"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10421",
   "text": "whom you were to protect;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10422",
   "text": "they will not get over your death,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10423",
   "text": "ever again."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10424",
   "text": "I think the world will sooner perish"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10425",
   "text": "than your like is born."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10426",
   "text": "You have lost your life here"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10427",
   "text": "for loyalty and for honour."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10428",
   "text": "God have mercy on you forever more.\""
  },
  {
   "ref": "10429",
   "text": "Then the Trojans cried out;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10430",
   "text": "they threw the banners"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10431",
   "text": "on the ground."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10432",
   "text": "From sorrow and from pain"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10433",
   "text": "they were all disheartened."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10434",
   "text": "Achilles came chasing after them;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10435",
   "text": "there were slain and trampled"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10436",
   "text": "five hundred before the city,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10437",
   "text": "who all fell"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10438",
   "text": "after Hector's fall."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10439",
   "text": "The land suffered harm from it,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10440",
   "text": "this great calamity"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10441",
   "text": "and many another hardship"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10442",
   "text": "that later came about for this cause:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10443",
   "text": "because Hector had fallen."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10444",
   "text": "The distress became so manifold"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10445",
   "text": "that I could not tell it"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10446",
   "text": "even if I had ten mouths."
  },
  {
   "ref": "10447",
   "text": "When Hector lay dead,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10448",
   "text": "many a worthy warrior lamented"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10449",
   "text": "because their lord lay dead;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "10450",
   "text": "the whole land was struck with dread,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11258",
   "text": "ever, for my sake."
  },
  {
   "ref": "11259",
   "text": "I must always be well disposed to you;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11260",
   "text": "you have well deserved that."
  },
  {
   "ref": "11261",
   "text": "You were always close to me."
  },
  {
   "ref": "11262",
   "text": "So [help] you God, now see"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11263",
   "text": "how I set about my course:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11264",
   "text": "unless Polyxena becomes mine,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11265",
   "text": "nothing else is left for it"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11266",
   "text": "but that I take my own life."
  },
  {
   "ref": "11267",
   "text": "Now go away quickly,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "11268",
   "text": "so that I may keep my life,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13201",
   "text": "the Greeks with clamour,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13202",
   "text": "the others for the fall,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13203",
   "text": "because Troilus was slain."
  },
  {
   "ref": "13204",
   "text": "He fell dead on the grass,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13205",
   "text": "all hacked to pieces."
  },
  {
   "ref": "13206",
   "text": "At that the ladies cried out"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13534",
   "text": "Achilles started up from his sleep."
  },
  {
   "ref": "13535",
   "text": "When he understood the message,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13536",
   "text": "he quickly stood up."
  },
  {
   "ref": "13537",
   "text": "Fondly he thought of him:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "13538",
   "text": "he woke Antilochus,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15626",
   "text": "those who had never seen it."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15627",
   "text": "As long as we have the image here"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15628",
   "text": "within our moats,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15629",
   "text": "we will hold it for certain"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15630",
   "text": "that our city will not come to grief."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15631",
   "text": "I do not know what more to say."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15632",
   "text": "Pallas sent it here;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15633",
   "text": "it is called the Palladium."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15634",
   "text": "We worship it in here"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15635",
   "text": "with affection and with love"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15636",
   "text": "and with great honours."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15637",
   "text": "As for our being captured:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15638",
   "text": "as long as this image is in here"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15639",
   "text": "there is no stratagem for it"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15838",
   "text": "and they all believed"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15839",
   "text": "that it would go well."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15840",
   "text": "Very late that night,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15841",
   "text": "when people had gone to bed,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15842",
   "text": "Antenor went into the temple"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15843",
   "text": "where the priest Theanus"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15844",
   "text": "guarded their sacred object,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15845",
   "text": "which was called the Palladium —"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15846",
   "text": "though it may rather have been the devil;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15847",
   "text": "we have read much about it,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15848",
   "text": "what wonders came of it."
  },
  {
   "ref": "15849",
   "text": "Antenor said to the priest,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15850",
   "text": "\"You have clearly seen today"
  },
  {
   "ref": "15851",
   "text": "what has happened to our sacrifice,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17629",
   "text": "She had a peculiar nature,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17630",
   "text": "and a life unlike other women's."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17631",
   "text": "Circe knew how to give potions,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17632",
   "text": "such magic, such food,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17633",
   "text": "that there was never anyone so wise"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17634",
   "text": "who tasted of her things —"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17635",
   "text": "I have tried it until I know it;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17636",
   "text": "I say this in truth —"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17637",
   "text": "[but] he was caught in such a snare"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17638",
   "text": "that he had to stay in it."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17639",
   "text": "She could work wonders."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17640",
   "text": "I must tell still more of her:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17641",
   "text": "she had such a greeting,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17642",
   "text": "such bearing, such words,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17643",
   "text": "that whoever had heard it"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17644",
   "text": "as I have heard it"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17645",
   "text": "would have had to stay there forever."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17646",
   "text": "I say nothing of all her magic arts:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17647",
   "text": "Circe is so made by nature"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17648",
   "text": "that she wants man after man;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17649",
   "text": "no one can guard himself"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17650",
   "text": "from having to stay there"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17651",
   "text": "with her and with her women."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17652",
   "text": "She gave me drink; when I had drunk,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17653",
   "text": "I had, against my will,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17654",
   "text": "to think of her love."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17655",
   "text": "My thoughts were fixed"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17656",
   "text": "from then on, at all times, on her;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17657",
   "text": "I could never forget her."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17658",
   "text": "When I had eaten her food,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17659",
   "text": "I forgot all the women"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17660",
   "text": "I had ever known before."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17661",
   "text": "The more often I looked at her,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17662",
   "text": "the more pleasing the sight was to me."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17663",
   "text": "Why say more? It happened to me"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17664",
   "text": "as it had happened to many."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17665",
   "text": "I will also grant her this:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17666",
   "text": "no sweeter woman was ever born."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17667",
   "text": "She had chosen me for it, too,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17668",
   "text": "and said that I was"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17669",
   "text": "the best lover"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17670",
   "text": "who had ever lain with her."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17671",
   "text": "I stayed there many a day."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17672",
   "text": "Hear how I came away from there:"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17673",
   "text": "my heart took me from myself;"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17674",
   "text": "from this I know well that magic"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17675",
   "text": "is a wind against a man's heart."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17676",
   "text": "I held to my manhood"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17677",
   "text": "and left the softness"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17678",
   "text": "that had led me astray."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17679",
   "text": "However unwillingly I did it,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17680",
   "text": "my heart did a hard thing."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17681",
   "text": "Neither magic, poison nor entreaty"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17682",
   "text": "could hold me back."
  },
  {
   "ref": "17683",
   "text": "I left it to God's will"
  },
  {
   "ref": "17684",
   "text": "and turned away from there and went on"
  },
  {
   "ref": "18272",
   "text": "Then he built a stronghold"
  },
  {
   "ref": "18273",
   "text": "such that he knew well"
  },
  {
   "ref": "18274",
   "text": "that had all the world come there,"
  },
  {
   "ref": "18275",
   "text": "they could not have taken him there."
  },
  {
   "ref": "18276",
   "text": "It has been told above"
  }
 ]
}